I was hanging out with the cool kids in rec.games.roguelike.nethack when 
Veloso got out a spraycan and scrawled the following:
>  * New attribute "keen memory" with the following effects:
>    * spell memorization decays at 2/3 the normal rate

If anything, I'd increase the effect on spell timeout.  But that's because I'm
a slow player.

>    * immunity from the amnesia effects of scrolls of amnesia and
>      tentacle attack

As others have said, probably too unbalancing.  With a unihorn and one of these
rings, a mind flayer would be very little threat at all.

>  * Intrinsic keen memory when polymorphed into a mumak or mastodon
>    * (An elephant never forgets)

I like that one.  A nice touch that's *nearly* too awkward for anyone to bother
using it.


How about having different enchantment levels?  +0 has no effect (except for
the usual nutrition cost), negative causes faster spell timeouts, positive
slows down the timeouts and reduces the amnesia effects.  And something
excessive like +5, which would require multiple attempts at enchantment, gives
you complete immunity.

